#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:2
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:5
msgid ""
"PyBaMM is available on GNU/Linux, MacOS and Windows. It can be installed "
"using ``uv``, ``pip``, or ``conda``, or from source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:9
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:11
msgid "To use PyBaMM, you must have Python 3.10 - 3.14 installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:15
msgid ""
"To install Python 3 on Debian-based distributions (Debian, Ubuntu), open a "
"terminal and run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:17
msgid ""
"sudo apt-get update\n"
"sudo apt-get install python3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:24
msgid ""
"On macOS, you can use the ``homebrew`` package manager. First, `install brew "
"<https://docs.python-guide.org/starting/install3/osx/>`__:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:27
msgid ""
"ruby -e \"$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/"
"HEAD/install.sh)\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:31
msgid ""
"then follow instructions in the link on adding ``brew`` to path, and run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:33
msgid "brew install python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:39
msgid ""
"To install Python 3, download the installation files from `Python's website "
"<https://www.python.org/downloads/windows/>`__. Make sure to tick the box on "
"``Add Python 3.X to PATH``. For more detailed instructions please see the "
"`official Python on Windows guide <https://docs.python.org/3/using/windows."
"html>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:48
msgid "Virtual environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:50
msgid ""
"We recommend installing PyBaMM within a virtual environment, in order not to "
"alter any distribution Python files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:53
msgid "To create a virtual environment within your current directory:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:57
msgid "uv venv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:61
msgid ""
"This creates a ``.venv`` directory. You can then \"activate\" the "
"environment using:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:65
msgid "source .venv/bin/activate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:71
msgid ".venv\\Scripts\\activate.bat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:79
msgid "virtualenv env"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:83
#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:103
msgid "You can then \"activate\" the environment using:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:85
msgid "source env/bin/activate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:91
msgid "First install ``virtualenv``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:93
msgid "python -m pip install virtualenv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:97
msgid "Then create a virtual environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:99
msgid "python -m virtualenv env"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:105
msgid "env\\Scripts\\activate.bat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:109
msgid ""
"When you are ready to exit the environment and go back to your original "
"system, just type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:111
msgid "deactivate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/index.rst:115
msgid ""
"For an introduction to virtual environments, see (https://realpython.com/"
"python-virtual-environments-a-primer/)."
msgstr ""

